{% doc %}
  Shared brand logo: picks the right image for the active color preset and
  outputs ONE <img>. Outputs nothing when no logo is configured — every caller
  must supply its own text fallback (shop.name / brand name).

  Why Liquid instead of CSS: switching a theme preset changes color values in
  settings_data.json, not a media query, so CSS cannot know which logo to show.
  A customer-side color switch was declined (2026-11-12), so the server always
  knows the active palette and there is no need to emit both images.

  ⚠️ The 128 threshold MUST stay in sync with `snippets/css-variables.liquid`
  (header_luma): that file uses the same number to pick the header surface
  color. If the two drift apart, a dark header can be paired with the
  light-background logo. Both use `color_brightness` (0–255, 128 = midpoint)
  and fall back to 255 when the color cannot be read.

  @param {string} [logo_class] - Class on the generated img element
  @param {number} [logo_width] - Base width passed to image_url
  @param {string} [logo_widths] - Comma separated widths for the image_tag srcset
  @param {string} [logo_sizes] - sizes attribute
  @param {string} [logo_alt] - Alt text; pass an empty string for decorative images
  @param {string} [logo_loading] - "lazy" or "eager"

  @example
  {% render 'brand-logo', logo_class: 'main-nav__logo-img' %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign skeleton_bg = settings.skeleton_background_color | default: settings.background_color
  assign skeleton_luma = skeleton_bg | color_brightness | default: 255

  assign brand_logo = settings.logo
  if skeleton_luma <= 128 and settings.logo_dark != blank
    assign brand_logo = settings.logo_dark
  endif

  assign img_width = logo_width | default: 160
  assign img_widths = logo_widths | default: '80, 120, 160, 240'
  assign img_sizes = logo_sizes | default: '40px'
  assign img_alt = logo_alt | default: ''
  assign img_loading = logo_loading | default: 'eager'
-%}

{%- if brand_logo != blank -%}
  {{
    brand_logo
    | image_url: width: img_width
    | image_tag:
      widths: img_widths,
      sizes: img_sizes,
      alt: img_alt,
      loading: img_loading,
      class: logo_class
  }}
{%- endif -%}
